meta {
  name: replace time off
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

put {
  url: {{base_url}}/administrator/time-off/:id/
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: c4e8a1b7-2d95-4f30-8a16-9b7c3e5d2f48
}

body:json {
  {
    // Required. Which teacher this window belongs to.
    "teacher": "1e54776b-9910-4742-9f8c-8efd23912d4a",
    // Required, ISO-8601 with offset.
    "start_datetime": "2026-12-24T00:00:00-05:00",
    // Required, and must be after start_datetime.
    "end_datetime": "2027-01-02T00:00:00-05:00",

    // Optional; omitting clears it.
    "reason": "Christmas holidays"
  }
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  `PUT` **replaces** the record: any writable field you leave out is reset to its
  default or blank, not left alone. Use `PATCH` (see **update time off**) unless you are
  deliberately sending the whole object -- an edit form that omits a field will
  silently wipe it.

  All three of `teacher`, `start_datetime` and `end_datetime` are required, and
  the end must be after the start.

  ## API example response
  {
    "id": "c4e8a1b7-2d95-4f30-8a16-9b7c3e5d2f48",
    "teacher": "1e54776b-9910-4742-9f8c-8efd23912d4a",
    "start_datetime": "2026-12-24T00:00:00-05:00",
    "end_datetime": "2027-01-02T00:00:00-05:00",
    "reason": "Christmas holidays",
    "created_at": "2026-09-05T09:20:00.000000-05:00"
  }
}
